// "[subject] draws N" ([CR#121.1]): the DECLARATIVE-SUBJECT draw — that player
// draws N cards, ONE AT A TIME ([CR#121.2] — a per-card sequence, NOT a
// simultaneous batch like mill). The keyword action as DATA, the twin of
// `Mills`: a `Composite` whose tag is `Draw(who, n)` and whose body DESCRIBES
// the top-N Library → Hand relocation (an `Each` per-card move). `who`
// (Param(0)) rides BOTH the atom and the body selection's `whose`. The engine
// does NOT run the body — it emits N single-card `Act(Draw)` attempts, each
// binding the library top LATE and empty-checking BEFORE its move (an empty
// library loses the game, [CR#120.3,104.3c]).
//
// The template renders the subject context-aware ("Target player draws two
// cards.", "Each player draws a card."); the count spells its noun via the
// `card|cards` modifier.
//
// Usage: Draws(It, 1) (the announced player target / Each-bound player, Jace
// Beleren) / Draws(Target(0), 2).
(
    name: "Draws",
    template: "${0} draws ${1:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Reference, Count],
    body: Composite(
        Draw(Param(0), Param(1)),
        Each(binder: Existing(TopOfLibrary(count: Param(1), whose: Param(0))), effect: Move(It, Hand)),
    ),
)
